@startuml
title Specified Functional Requirements - Sequence Diagram
autonumber

actor User <<Visitor>>
actor "Registered User" as RegisteredUser <<RegisteredUser>>
actor Admin <<Administrator>>
participant "Postman / API Client" as Client
participant "Massage Reservation API" as API
participant "Authentication Middleware" as Auth
participant "Authentication Controller" as AuthController
participant "Shop Controller" as ShopController
participant "Reservation Controller" as ReservationController
database MongoDB

== Register ==
User -> Client: Submit name, telephone, email, password
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/register
API -> AuthController: register
AuthController -> MongoDB: Validate and create user\n(hash password)
MongoDB --> AuthController: New registered user
AuthController --> API: User details and access token
API --> Client: Registration successful
Client --> User: Show account and token

== Log in ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Enter email and password
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/login
API -> AuthController: login
AuthController -> MongoDB: Find user and password hash
MongoDB --> AuthController: User record
AuthController -> AuthController: Verify password and issue JWT
AuthController --> API: Access token
API --> Client: Login successful
Client --> RegisteredUser: Store token

== Browse shops ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Request massage shop list
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/shops
API -> ShopController: getShops
ShopController -> MongoDB: Read shop information
MongoDB --> ShopController: Names, addresses, telephone,\nopening and closing times
ShopController --> API: Shop list
API --> Client: 200 OK with shop list
Client --> RegisteredUser: Display shops

== Make a reservation ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Choose shop, date, and start time
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/reservations\n(Bearer token, shopId, date, startTime)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and load user
Auth -> MongoDB: Find user and check token version
MongoDB --> Auth: Authenticated user
Auth --> API: Continue as registered user
API -> ReservationController: createReservation
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Validate shop and operating hours
MongoDB --> ReservationController: Shop exists and is open
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Count user's confirmed reservations
alt Fewer than 3 active reservations
    MongoDB --> ReservationController: Limit not reached
    ReservationController -> MongoDB: Create confirmed reservation
    MongoDB --> ReservationController: Reservation
    ReservationController --> API: 201 Created
    API --> Client: Reservation details
    Client --> RegisteredUser: Show confirmation
else Already has 3 active reservations
    MongoDB --> ReservationController: Limit reached
    ReservationController --> API: 400 Reservation limit reached
    API --> Client: Error response
    Client --> RegisteredUser: Show limit message
end

== View own reservations ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Request my reservations
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/reservations\n(Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth -> MongoDB: Find user and check token version
MongoDB --> Auth: Authenticated user
Auth --> API: Continue as registered user
API -> ReservationController: getMyReservations
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Find reservations for this user
MongoDB --> ReservationController: User's reservations
ReservationController --> API: Reservation list
API --> Client: 200 OK
Client --> RegisteredUser: Display reservations

== Edit or delete own reservation ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Edit reservation fields
Client -> API: PUT /api/v1/reservations/{id}\n(Bearer token, updated fields)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> ReservationController: updateReservation
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Update only owner's reservation
MongoDB --> ReservationController: Updated reservation or not found
ReservationController --> API: Update result
API --> Client: 200 OK or error

RegisteredUser -> Client: Delete own reservation
Client -> API: DELETE /api/v1/reservations/{id}\n(Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> ReservationController: deleteReservation
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Delete only owner's reservation
MongoDB --> ReservationController: Deleted reservation or not found
ReservationController --> API: Delete result
API --> Client: 200 OK or error

== Admin manages any reservation ==
Admin -> Client: Log in with email and password
Client -> API: POST /api/v1/auth/login
API -> AuthController: Verify credentials and issue JWT
AuthController -> MongoDB: Find admin and verify password
MongoDB --> AuthController: Admin account
AuthController --> API: Admin access token
API --> Client: Login successful

Admin -> Client: View all reservations
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/reservations\n(Admin Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth -> MongoDB: Find admin and check token version
MongoDB --> Auth: Admin account
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ReservationController: getMyReservations
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Find all reservations
MongoDB --> ReservationController: All reservations
ReservationController --> API: Reservation list
API --> Client: 200 OK

Admin -> Client: Edit or delete any reservation
Client -> API: PUT or DELETE /api/v1/reservations/{id}
API -> Auth: Verify JWT and admin role
Auth --> API: Continue as admin
API -> ReservationController: Update or delete reservation
ReservationController -> MongoDB: Apply admin operation to reservation
MongoDB --> ReservationController: Operation result
ReservationController --> API: Result
API --> Client: 200 OK or error

== Log out ==
RegisteredUser -> Client: Log out
Client -> API: GET /api/v1/auth/logout\n(Bearer token)
API -> Auth: Verify JWT
Auth --> API: Authenticated user
API -> AuthController: logout
AuthController -> MongoDB: Increment tokenVersion
MongoDB --> AuthController: Session revoked
AuthController --> API: Clear cookie and confirm
API --> Client: Logout successful
Client --> RegisteredUser: Clear local token

note over Client, API
    Requests can be exercised with Postman.
end note
@enduml
